CORE libstdcxx13
harness.cpp
--cpp17 -I ../../../src --object-bits 12 --unwind 8 --no-unwinding-assertions
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
FAILURE
--
Unit proof for string2optional_int: round trip, stoll PREFIX semantics
(trailing junk ignored) and nullopt for digit-less input, through the
wrap_string_conversion layer (lambda + catch of std::invalid_argument).
g++/clang++ accept the harness and it verifies at runtime.
libstdcxx13: with GCC 11's headers std::from_chars (__from_chars_digit,
with __builtin_mul_overflow) made the SAT problem exceed 7 GB, also with
-99..99 and --unwind 5 (Ubuntu 22.04 and 32-bit CI jobs).
